\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"31cfec89bb7f058ffa7c8ed39148574896a31698d86778eee49821d27e536c42","event_uuid":"348ccc42-01ac-4111-81e2-e780c8587c99","position":{"commit_sha":"9e85e0dcc388ae83f0b8f8dc8dfbb4e50bbec0bb","position":"1786928010627036001-348ccc42-01ac-4111-81e2-e780c8587c99"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (rebar-debug fast path)\n\nConfirmed root cause: `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py:143` calls `TarFile.extractall(extracted)` with neither a `filter=` argument nor a class extraction filter. On CPython 3.12.13, `_get_filter_function(None)` deterministically emits the reported `DeprecationWarning` before extracting anything; `pytest -W error::DeprecationWarning tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py::test_install_from_sdist_preserves_commit` failed at that exact branch. The introducing test commit is 5514923afe.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof: installing `tarfile.data_filter` as the process-wide default while leaving the test unchanged made the same warning-as-error reproduction pass (1 passed), ruling out the build backend and provenance round-trip as causes. The generated sdist contains exactly five relative regular files, all mode 0644, with no links or special entries. Applying `data_filter` rejected none and changed only uid/gid/uname/gname to None; the unchanged rebuild and exact `abc1234` provenance assertion passed. Python 3.11/3.12 tarfile documentation explicitly recommends setting `filter` according to needed features and says `filter=\"data\"` prevents the most dangerous extraction issues. Repository prior art uses the same policy in `scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py:214` and `scripts/mutation_gate.py:519`.\n\nDefect legitimacy: defect. The ticket acceptance contract requires the named test to pass with this warning promoted to an error and requires an explicit justified extraction policy. The smallest restoration is test-only `filter=\"data\"`, matching Python 3.14’s safe default; it changes no production archive behavior.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is explicit safe extraction of the self-generated sdist with the exact provenance round-trip unchanged. This extractall call is local to one pytest test and has no callers or consumers that depend on the warning or on ownership restoration. No behavioral dependency blocks repair.","timestamp":1786922382582618001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report\n\nProblem: `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py::test_install_from_sdist_preserves_commit` deterministically emitted Python’s future-default tar extraction warning.\n\nProven root cause: `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py:146` reached CPython 3.12.13 `TarFile._get_filter_function(None)` because the extractall call omitted `filter=` and no class extraction filter was configured. That exact runtime branch emitted the warning before extraction.\n\nProof: promoting DeprecationWarning to an error reproduced the failure. Installing `tarfile.data_filter` as the runtime default while leaving the test unchanged made the same scenario pass, ruling out the build backend and provenance path. The generated sdist had five relative regular files, all 0644, no links/special entries; `data_filter` rejected none and changed only ownership fields to None. The exact rebuild and `COMMIT == \"abc1234\"` assertion remained green.\n\nTest: the existing real-build integration test now carries a narrow pytest filterwarnings marker for this exact warning. Its final form was RED before the fix, was physically withheld from the fixer, then GREEN after repair. Removing only `filter=\"data\"` returned it to RED; restoring the fix returned it to GREEN. It asserts observable warning/build/wheel behavior and survives internal refactors.\n\nFix: `TarFile.extractall(extracted, filter=\"data\")`, matching Python’s safe future default, plus the exact warning-as-error regression guard. No production code, dependency, fixture, or existing provenance assertion changed.\n\nScope and safety: the call site is local to one test and has no caller that depends on implicit extraction, ownership restoration, or the warning. This restores forward-compatible test behavior, creates no product capability, adds no dependency, and weakens no test.\n\nSiblings: a repository-wide `extractall(` sweep found no other omitted-filter instance. The four remaining sites use `data` or a stricter hardened filter. Parity sweep is N/A: this is a single test fixture, not a multi-channel product operation.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: (accepted) CPython 3.11.0–3.11.3 predate the security backport for `filter=`; they are superseded patch levels, and `src/rebar/llm/workflow/snapshot.py:56-66` already refuses safe snapshot extraction there. (ticket filed) `fleeting-choosey-dore` owns the zizmor offline-mode warning. (ticket filed) `illegible-principal-grayfox` owns duplicate structured-output candidate warnings and carries an RP-01 coordination guard. Other full-suite warnings already have active owners: `ferrety-crippling-dairycow`, `stumpy-cinnabar-basenji`, and `dragonish-sylphic-sheep`.\n\nReplication and gates: exact original command passed (1 passed); focused file passed (7 passed); `make lint` and `make typecheck` passed; `make test` passed with 13,527 passed, 60 skipped, 289 deselected. Local `rebar review-code` passed with zero findings. Gerrit 1833 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero comments, then merged as 81c3e9ec86d5fda18258e53e9fc9887d86251f45.","timestamp":1786927527331499001}],"created_at":1786914857540797001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6c267e00-d2a2-498e-8904-ae1d2f5db2a7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc"},{"link_uuid":"e86f43a2-4f1a-4c95-96f8-c0ad186a9d3e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"faff-0415-df1b-400c"},{"link_uuid":"64df2890-2ae7-48fd-969c-256f37d79546","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7674-00ad-5df0-4f5f"},{"link_uuid":"f7615915-b858-49c1-bac6-e162ef1b948c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e20b-207b-82a2-4ec9"},{"link_uuid":"348ccc42-01ac-4111-81e2-e780c8587c99","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"6168-df06-1e08-4ea3"}],"description":"## Context\nThe default test suite passes but `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py::test_install_from_sdist_preserves_commit` emits Python's `DeprecationWarning` at line 143: Python 3.14 will filter extracted tar archives by default and may reject files or modify metadata. The test calls `TarFile.extractall(extracted)` without an explicit `filter=` policy.\n\n## Reproduction\nRun the named test with warnings enabled under the repository virtualenv. The warning is deterministic on Python 3.12 and identifies the future 3.14 behavior change.\n\n## Plan\nUse rebar-debug to establish the intended safe extraction policy and prove whether the test fixture requires metadata that a standard filter changes. Apply the smallest compatibility repair with a RED warning-as-error oracle; do not weaken archive-safety behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The named build-provenance test runs with its tar extraction warning promoted to an error and passes.\n- [x] The selected extraction filter is explicit and justified against the fixture's required metadata.\n- [x] Existing build-provenance assertions remain unchanged or stronger.\n- [x] The focused test and repository gates pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py","reason":"Make the test fixture choose Python tarfile data extraction explicitly while preserving its provenance assertions."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7674-00ad-5df0-4f5f"],["relates_to","e20b-207b-82a2-4ec9"],["relates_to","faff-0415-df1b-400c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"716b19d0-f4b1-400e-b790-a0ad41323ff6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["warning","python314","tests"],"ticket_id":"e06a-1450-5e1b-42fc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Python 3.14 tar extraction warning in build-provenance test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8acdbf2c-d194-402c-ab17-7cabdddfc5a1","b47dac49-0dea-4b2f-987c-d16fba4680a0","e86f43a2-4f1a-4c95-96f8-c0ad186a9d3e","18848b86-e6d7-401e-9477-e6f17d0f7ddb","e64bf086-8902-4ed5-b078-2cbe576676b3","27e4769b-f84f-4219-a293-0ea619635eed","8e7f712a-fb08-4a26-9bce-912270130ca8","64df2890-2ae7-48fd-969c-256f37d79546","f7615915-b858-49c1-bac6-e162ef1b948c","7cffbcf4-f883-4eb9-be25-5f66d68c7d31","d2b46d11-c131-46ed-9020-56864ff042b8","716b19d0-f4b1-400e-b790-a0ad41323ff6","6e94b15b-a9bf-4b86-8113-2fac14774dc2","348ccc42-01ac-4111-81e2-e780c8587c99"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786932081129412001,"uuid":"ce78aea3-7303-45fb-9802-eace0aeac96e"}